      "data": {
        "text": "\"Create presigned_download.py in the current working directory.\nTask: creates a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object.\nUse one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99d480f001rXMaGwaddwQ0Cd",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99d480b001wC6PREuF43meyw",
      "session_id": "ses_f4662b7fcffeDEuhceYc30Gnpk",
      "time_created": 1789820487695,
      "time_updated": 1789820487696
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "type": "step-start"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99d4d47001VnWyyJrMSEtBm6",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99d4812001bUCn5vZEkhPkk7",
      "session_id": "ses_f4662b7fcffeDEuhceYc30Gnpk",
      "time_created": 1789820489031,
      "time_updated": 1789820489031
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing the Cloud Provider**\n\nI'm zeroing in on Amazon S3 as the external provider. Its familiarity and widespread use make it a logical choice for implementing the presigned download URL generation. I'll need to make sure the S3 identifier is baked into the Python code to ensure that I'm implementing my chosen provider and not a placeholder.\n\n\n**Defining the Script's Function**\n\nI'm now outlining the structure of `presigned_download.py`. The script will leverage `boto3` to generate the presigned URL. The core components will be placeholders for AWS credentials, region, bucket name, object key, and URL expiration time. The user should be able to input these.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820492436,
          "start": 1789820489038
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99d4d4e001SKuYgk4Sb5L4t9",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99d4812001bUCn5vZEkhPkk7",
      "session_id": "ses_f4662b7fcffeDEuhceYc30Gnpk",
      "time_created": 1789820489038,
      "time_updated": 1789820492437
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "5jpQgo2IXho1GNBI",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ndef create_presigned_url(bucket_name, object_name, expiration=3600):\n    \"\"\"Generate a presigned URL to share an S3 object\n\n    :param bucket_name: String\n    :param object_name: String\n    :param expiration: Time in seconds for the presigned URL to remain valid\n    :return: Presigned URL as string. If error, returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Replace with your AWS credentials and region\n    # It's recommended to use environment variables or IAM roles for production\n    aws_access_key_id = \"YOUR_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\"\n    aws_secret_access_key = \"YOUR_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\"\n    aws_region = \"YOUR_AWS_REGION\" # e.g., \"us-east-1\"\n\n    s3_client = boto3.client(\n        \"s3\",\n        aws_access_key_id=aws_access_key_id,\n        aws_secret_access_key=aws_secret_access_key,\n        region_name=aws_region\n    )\n    try:\n        response = s3_client.generate_presigned_url(\n            \"get_object\",\n            Params={\"Bucket\": bucket_name, \"Key\": object_name},\n            ExpiresIn=expiration,\n        )\n    except ClientError as e:\n        print(e)\n        return None\n\n    # The response contains the presigned URL\n    return response\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    bucket = \"YOUR_S3_BUCKET_NAME\"\n    object = \"YOUR_S3_OBJECT_KEY\" # e.g., \"myfolder/myfile.txt\"\n\n    if \"YOUR_S3_BUCKET_NAME\" in bucket or \"YOUR_S3_OBJECT_KEY\" in object:\n        print(\"Please replace 'YOUR_S3_BUCKET_NAME' and 'YOUR_S3_OBJECT_KEY' with your actual S3 bucket and object key.\")\n        print(\"Also, replace 'YOUR_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID', 'YOUR_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY', and 'YOUR_AWS_REGION' with your AWS credentials and region.\")\n    else:\n        url = create_presigned_url(bucket, object)\n        if url:\n            print(f\"Presigned URL: {url}\")\n        else:\n            print(\"Could not generate presigned URL.\")\n",
            "filePath": "presigned_download.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
