    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing S3 for File Upload**\n\nI've decided to use Amazon S3 as the object storage provider for the Python script. It's a prevalent choice, which simplifies integration and documentation. Now, I'm focusing on how to integrate the S3 functionality within `upload_object.py`.\n\n\n**Defining S3 Integration**\n\nI'm now integrating S3 functionality within `upload_object.py`. I'll create a function with the file path/byte stream, bucket, and object name as parameters. `boto3` will handle the S3 upload. I'll include `boto3` import and `s3_client` instantiation to make the provider clear.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820486846,
          "start": 1789820485266
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99d3e92001SOhcP1RXT5m2jr",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99d38cb0016Za7cticMzvJsY",
      "session_id": "ses_f4662c7b8ffe2nrJXmEScr2AyF",
      "time_created": 1789820485266,
      "time_updated": 1789820486846
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "YPEFKUQ6UxNv0pez",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef upload_object(bucket_name, object_name, file_path=None, data_stream=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Uploads a file or byte stream to an S3 bucket.\n\n    :param bucket_name: Name of the S3 bucket.\n    :param object_name: S3 object name (key).\n    :param file_path: Path to the file to upload.\n    :param data_stream: Byte stream to upload.\n    \"\"\"\n    s3_client = boto3.client('s3')\n\n    if file_path:\n        if not os.path.exists(file_path):\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"The file {file_path} does not exist.\")\n        s3_client.upload_file(file_path, bucket_name, object_name)\n        print(f\"File '{file_path}' uploaded to '{bucket_name}/{object_name}'\")\n    elif data_stream:\n        s3_client.put_object(Bucket=bucket_name, Key=object_name, Body=data_stream)\n        print(f\"Byte stream uploaded to '{bucket_name}/{object_name}'\")\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"Either 'file_path' or 'data_stream' must be provided.\")\n\n",
            "filePath": "upload_object.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
            "filepath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-_bc3k7n5/upload_object.py",
            "truncated": false
